<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea supplies 1.7 trln won to banks.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea supplies 1.7 trln won to banks.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Korea supplied 1.7 trillion won to commercial banks on Tuesday, by allowing the banks to cash in repurchase agreements ahead of maturity to ease liquidity shortage, an official at the central bank said.  </p>
<p>He said banks were suffering from liquidity shortage as they were due to face the central bank's bi-monthly review of won reserve levels on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The repurchase agreements were originally due to mature on Wednesday, he said.</p>
<p>He gave no further information.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
